<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea to borrow $1.49 bln for facility purchases.</title>
<headline>S.Korea to borrow $1.49 bln for facility purchases.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea said on Friday it had given approval to 29 companies to borrow $1.49 billion in foreign exchange loans in the second half of this year to buy capital goods.</p>
<p>The finance ministry said a total of 30 companies were permitted to borrow $1.2 billion in the first half for capital purchases.</p>
<p>Korea Electric Power Corp (KEPCO) was approved to borrow $200 million, Pohang Iron and Steel Co (POSCO) $165 million and Dacom Corp $100 million.</p>
</text>
